Use the graph to solve $y=x+2$ and $y=-x+6$ simultaneously. Verify that the intersection satisfies both equations.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{seriesBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{seriesRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[draw=black!20,xstep=10mm,ystep=10mm] (-1,-1) grid (5,7);
\draw[<->,black] (-1.3,0)--(5.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.3)--(0,7.3) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-1,1,2,3,4,5} {\draw[black] (\v,0.07)--(\v,-0.07);\path (\v,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-1,1,2,3,4,5,6,7} {\draw[black] (0.07,\v)--(-0.07,\v);\path (-0.1,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\path (-0.1,-0.1) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[seriesBlue,thick,<->] (-1,1)--(5,7);
\draw[seriesRed,thick,dashed,<->] (-1,7)--(5,1);
\path (4,6.3) node[above left,text=seriesBlue] {$y=x+2$};
\path (4,1.7) node[below left,text=seriesRed] {$y=-x+6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the graph to solve $y=2x-2$ and $y=4$ simultaneously.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{seriesBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{seriesRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[draw=black!20,xstep=10mm,ystep=10mm] (-1,-3) grid (5,6);
\draw[<->,black] (-1.3,0)--(5.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-3.3)--(0,6.3) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-1,1,2,3,4,5} {\draw[black] (\v,0.07)--(\v,-0.07);\path (\v,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (0.07,\v)--(-0.07,\v);\path (-0.1,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\path (-0.1,-0.1) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[seriesBlue,thick,<->] (-0.5,-3)--(4,6);
\draw[seriesRed,thick,dashed,<->] (-1,4)--(5,4);
\path (3.4,5.5) node[left,text=seriesBlue] {$y=2x-2$};
\path (4.9,4.1) node[above left,text=seriesRed] {$y=4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the graph to solve $y=-x+2$ and $x=-2$ simultaneously.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{seriesBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{seriesRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[draw=black!20,xstep=10mm,ystep=10mm] (-4,-2) grid (3,6);
\draw[<->,black] (-4.3,0)--(3.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-2.3)--(0,6.3) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw[black] (\v,0.07)--(\v,-0.07);\path (\v,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (0.07,\v)--(-0.07,\v);\path (-0.1,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\path (-0.1,-0.1) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[seriesBlue,thick,<->] (-4,6)--(3,-1);
\draw[seriesRed,thick,dashed,<->] (-2,-2)--(-2,6);
\path (1,1.3) node[above right,text=seriesBlue] {$y=-x+2$};
\path (-2.1,5.7) node[left,text=seriesRed] {$x=-2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shows $y=x+1$ and $y=x-2$. How many simultaneous solutions do they have? Explain using the graph.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{seriesBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{seriesRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[draw=black!20,xstep=10mm,ystep=10mm] (-3,-4) grid (3,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.3,0)--(3.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-4.3)--(0,4.3) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw[black] (\v,0.07)--(\v,-0.07);\path (\v,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw[black] (0.07,\v)--(-0.07,\v);\path (-0.1,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\path (-0.1,-0.1) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[seriesBlue,thick,<->] (-3,-2)--(3,4);
\draw[seriesRed,thick,dashed,<->] (-2,-4)--(3,1);
\path (1,2.3) node[above left,text=seriesBlue] {$y=x+1$};
\path (1,-1.3) node[below right,text=seriesRed] {$y=x-2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shows $y=x-1$ and $2y=2x-2$. How many simultaneous solutions do they have? Explain.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{seriesBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{seriesRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[draw=black!20,xstep=10mm,ystep=10mm] (-3,-4) grid (3,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.3,0)--(3.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-4.3)--(0,4.3) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw[black] (\v,0.07)--(\v,-0.07);\path (\v,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw[black] (0.07,\v)--(-0.07,\v);\path (-0.1,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
